MistyLoader is an AI-assisted experimental extension of llama.cpp and ggml.
The runtime is distributed as a patch against the exact upstream revision in
upstream.lock.json. Upstream copyright and MIT license terms are retained in
LICENSE and licenses/llama.cpp.txt. The bootstrap script fetches the upstream
source, including its original third-party notices.

Strata, by Niko1221 and the Strata contributors, inspired the hybrid expert
cache and concurrent CPU/GPU execution work. Strata was studied as a reference;
its installed runtime and model files are not included in this distribution.
Its MIT attribution is retained in licenses/Strata.txt.
Reference: https://github.com/attentiondotnet/Strata
Inspected revision: a0116b2782a5b82622358c04a06496485d12b2d6

Mistral AI created Mistral Small 4. The tested community GGUF was published by
timteh673. Exact model provenance and checksums are in configs/model-provenance.json.
Model weights, model-derived scale data, and CUDA runtime binaries are not
included in this source distribution. Models retain their own license terms.

Red Hat AI's Mistral Small 4 DFlash draft informed the deferred speculative
decoding experiment. No draft weights are included and speculation is disabled
in the released speed profile.

OpenAI Codex assisted with implementation, debugging, testing, documentation,
and benchmarking. This project is independent of the organizations credited
above; their inclusion does not imply endorsement.
